      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SECRET SERVICE AGENT NZ (9) is going about his business in good style with placings at his last three starts including a second most recently over 2190m at Maryborough, beaten a nose after leading. Drawn to enjoy an economical run and might sweat on the sprint lane. Recent efforts are good enough to put him right in the finish. ARZALI ROCKSTAR (1) saluted two starts ago at Ballarat but didn't measure up at her latest appearance over 1785m at Stawell, beaten 20 metres into tenth after being close to the pace throughout. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Big chance if she brings her A-game. CALEDONIAN RANGER (2) was responsible for a better effort last time out when third over 2200m at Ballarat. Should run a big race. YNOBE NOVA (5) is the best of the rest after finishing third over 1850m at Marburg last time out.",
